#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0105.1 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "THE SHEET'S OWN CASE (Fix #289 / M3-D6). DM declares NO SPECIES COLUMN AT ALL -- literally the Plain Text of rows 521-525, 'If species is not included in DM it must be included in TS or TX' -- and neither TS nor TX carries the parameter. The absent case was blocked TWICE before M3-D6: Requirements.Variables.All [SPECIES] skipped the rule before the Check ran, and NonEmptyGuardInliner's bare-emptiness arm would have added var_exists(\"SPECIES\") on top. Dropping the scope entry removes the first block and Fix #330's retirement of the emitter's bare-emptiness arm removes the second, so the bare empty(SPECIES) leaf is TRUE on every row of an absent column (absent = all-missing, EC-43) and the rule now reports the case its own sheet row leads with. M3-D6 originally authored an explicit `not var_exists(...) or empty(...)` disjunct here; Plan B phase 4d' deleted the now-redundant presence half, leaving the verdict unchanged. One DM row, so the count is 1 under every reading."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=001
dataset DM label="Demographics" class="SPECIAL PURPOSE"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SETCD   type=Char label="Set Code"
col SEX     type=Char label="Sex"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | SET01 | M
---

dataset TS label="Trial Summary" class="TRIAL DESIGN"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | TITLE  | Trial Title      | Study X
S1 | TS | 2 | SSTDTC | Study Start Date | 2023-01-01
---

dataset TX label="Trial Sets" class="TRIAL DESIGN"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col SETCD    type=Char label="Set Code"
col TXSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TXPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter Short Name"
col TXPARM   type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter"
col TXVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TX | SET01 | 1 | GRPLBL | Group Label | Control
---
